# vsftpd

## install
I looked on the wiki alpine and there are a few options for ftp. I chose vsftpd because it is the most secure.

In the Dockerfile I added the following lines:
```
RUN apk add vsftpd
```
and this is all we need. By default there is a configuration file in /etc/vsftpd/vsftpd.conf. This configuration file is quite strict and does not allow anonymous users to connect.

## docker compose

```yaml
  ftp:
    build: requirements/ftp
    env_file:       .env
    ports:
      - "21:21"
      - 30000-30009:30000-30009
    networks:
      - inception_network
    volumes:
      - wp-files:/var/www/html
    restart: on-failure
```

## ports
If translating the docker run commands to docker-compose files (which uses YAML format), note that YAML parses numbers in the format xx:yy as a base-60 value if the number is less than 60, so 21:21 must be specified as a quoted string.

